# Mobile scope

Read `mobile/.cursor/plans/mobile-login-spike.md` first. Implement that stage before `mobile/.cursor/plans/mobile-auth-screens.md`. Do not start a later slice until the previous slice's checks exist.

When a slice's checks finish, write `mobile/docs/slice-<number>-<name>.md` before the next slice. Record what was done, what was tested and the result, any failure and why, and what is next.

The app is for students on Android. Build only spec Section 10.2: login, register with email verification, activate, forgot-password and reset, a placeholder home, dev and prod flavors, secure tokens, a 401 refresh-and-retry, and Bangla plus English. English is the language on first launch.

Device exit is Shahriar's physical phone. The agent runs `flutter test` only. Do not install Android system images, create an AVD, or launch an emulator. For a phone run, hand over `flutter run --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=http://<lan-ip>:8080`. Keep `http://10.0.2.2:8080` as the in-app dev default. That URL is not a reason to start an emulator.

```dart
// BAD — user-facing copy inline
Text('Sign in')

// GOOD — catalog key, both locales
Text(t('auth.loginTitle'))
```

A wrong API field or token placement is an `api` defect. Fix `api` and its tests before adapting the client around it.
